# P41 on Windows, WinUIBackend: does a user edit of a SECONDS field reach the binding, and does nothing write back at launch? (2026-09-17; retargeted 2026-10-20)
#
# The 2026-09-17 version opened the seconds ComboBox beside the TimePicker of a `.wheel` + `.hourMinuteAndSecond` cell and expected `.hourMinuteAndSecond -> 2025-08-24 09:46:41`. That cell was replaced by `.clock`/`.rows` cells in b2573bfd, and on 2026-10-20 the TimePicker itself gave way to LocaleTimeRow, so the file clicked at a place where nothing of the kind exists. It now presses + on the seconds field of `.rows seconds`, measured 2026-10-20 with test_support/measure/measure_win.zsh: (688,1115) DIPs.
#
# TWO ASSERTIONS, both in p41-debug-events.log:
#   - before any input: no line containing ` -> ` at all. One there is the launch-time write-back defect (09:46:40 written back as 09:46:00 in 2026-09).
#   - after the press: exactly `.rows seconds -> 09:46:41`. Hours and minutes unchanged; only the seconds move, 40 -> 41.
#
# NEEDS A TALLER SCREEN: on a 1920x1080 display at 125% P41's window is 1471 px tall from y 32, so the .rows row (frame y 1115 DIPs = screen y 1490) is off screen and the click is clamped to y 1079 (measured 2026-10-20: the first assertion held -- no ` -> ` line --, the second could not be reached). Run it at 100% scaling or on a taller display.
#
# STILL OPEN, a different way, 2026-10-29: the row can now be reached -- P41 is in a ScrollView and SwiftCrossUI caps a window at the room on its screen (maximumSizeOnScreen), so the window ends above the taskbar (bottom 1019 at y 64) -- but scrolled to the bottom the + sits at a height that follows the window's, and WinUI cascades each new window 32 px down and right, so the window is 955, 923, 892 or 859 px depending on where it lands: the + was at (688,796) in a 1072 px window and (688,676) in a 892 px one. The click below is the 1072 px value and misses in a capped window. taplabel cannot aim at the seconds field (its "40" is a native TextBox, not a SwiftCrossUI Text). Needs a position that does not follow the window height.
# 2026-10-29 仍未解決，換了個樣子：那一列現在構得到了——P41 放進 ScrollView,SwiftCrossUI 也依視窗在螢幕上的空間封頂(maximumSizeOnScreen),視窗止於工作列上方(y 64 起，底部 1019)——但捲到底後 + 的高度跟著視窗高度走，而 WinUI 每開一個新視窗就往右下錯開 32 px,視窗依落點是 955、923、892 或 859 px:1072 px 的視窗中 + 在 (688,796),892 px 的在 (688,676)。下方的點擊是 1072 px 的值，在封頂後的視窗裡會點空。taplabel 也瞄不到秒數欄(它的「40」是原生 TextBox,不是 SwiftCrossUI 的 Text)。需要一個不隨視窗高度變動的位置。
# P41(Windows,WinUIBackend):使用者改秒數欄會不會抵達 binding,以及啟動時有沒有寫回?原本的目標格位(.wheel 加秒數)已在 b2573bfd 換成 .clock/.rows,TimePicker 也在 2026-10-20 換成 LocaleTimeRow,因此改按 `.rows seconds` 秒數欄的 +。通過:按之前 log 沒有任何 ` -> `,按之後恰為 `.rows seconds -> 09:46:41`。
sleep,,,,,,3000000,let the window settle; the launch-time assertion is read here,windows
move,1200,500,frame,,,,pointer over empty page space -- over the calendar the wheel turns its months instead,windows
scroll,0,10,,,,,ten notches down: P41 is in a ScrollView since 2026-10-29 and .rows is at the bottom,windows
sleep,,,,,,800000,,windows
click,688,796,frame,left,,,+ on the seconds field of .rows seconds -- 40 becomes 41,windows
sleep,,,,,,1500000,let the binding change reach the log,windows
